.TH piscou 1 "November 2026" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
piscou \- File previewer that executes a program according to a file's MIME type and/or filename.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B piscou
.I #piscou-file#
[#piscou-0# #piscou-1# ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B piscou
is a file previewer that executes a program based on a file's MIME type and/or filename. It is designed to be as fast as possible, and users can choose previewing programs with short startup times.

.PP
Users can pass up to 10 arguments to the program after the filename.

.SH BUILD REQUIREMENTS
A C11 compiler, pkg-config, and the libmagic development files are required.
The meta_regex source tree is optional on platforms supporting POSIX
.BR regex.h .
.SH REGEX BACKENDS
The build selects a regex backend using the
.B PISCOU_REGEX_BACKEND
environment variable:
.TP
.B auto
Default. Use meta_regex when the
.B meta_regex/
directory exists; otherwise use the POSIX libc backend.
.TP
.B meta
Require the full meta_regex source tree under
.BR meta_regex/src/ .
.TP
.B libc
Use POSIX
.B regex.h
even if meta_regex is present.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
PISCOU_REGEX_BACKEND=libc ./build.sh
PISCOU_REGEX_BACKEND=meta ./build.sh
.fi
.PP
If meta_regex is present but incomplete, automatic selection reports an
error. Forced libc mode does not require the meta_regex files. In meta_regex
mode, the build generates
.B gen/config2.h
with meta_preproc; libc mode includes
.B config.h
directly without preprocessing.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.P
Edit
.B config.h
and recompile. Note that by default,
.B piscou
might call programs that are not installed on your system.
.PP
Rules use the
.B R("pattern")
macro in either backend, including in static initializers. The two-argument
.B R("pattern", flags)
form is also supported, as are META_RE_NONE, META_RE_YESSUB, and
META_RE_NOSUB. Patterns may match a MIME type, filename, or both; at
least one matching field must be set.
.PP
The libc backend uses POSIX extended regular expressions (REG_EXTENDED).
PCRE-specific syntax is not supported there. The meta_regex implementation
may behave differently for some patterns or capture groups; prefer the
shared POSIX ERE subset for portable configurations.
.PP
The
.B #piscou-N#
placeholders select extra command-line arguments, including when embedded
within another argument. To compare both backends when meta_regex is
available, run
.BR ./tests/regex_backends.sh .

.SH LIMITATIONS
.P
All limitations are configurable via
.B config.h
. The default settings are:
.IP \(bu 4
Users can pass up to 10 "extra" arguments to
.B piscou
.IP \(bu 4
Users can pass up to 16 arguments to each program.
.IP \(bu 4
Each argument of those 16 can be up to 256 characters long.

.SH RATIONALE
.P
.B piscou
is designed to prioritize speed. It is recommended to choose previewing programs with short startup times.

.SH REPORTING BUGS
.P
Please report any bugs or issues on the
.B piscou
GitHub Issues page: https://github.com/lucas-mior/piscou/issues.
